          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-18502 utils: indent a multi-line value for get_param -y",
        "message": "LU-18502 utils: indent a multi-line value for get_param -y\n\nWith --yaml, \"lctl get_param\" prints the first line of a multi-line\nvalue on the line of the parameter name. When the value is a block\nmapping, a YAML parser rejects the output. A block mapping cannot\nstart on the line of its key.\n\nStart a multi-line value on the next line. Indent each line of the\nvalue by two spaces. A parser then reads the lines as the value of the\nparameter name.\n\nFixes: 5768bf35fd (\"LU-18502 utils: Support YAML for get_param parameter names\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-sec env=ONLY=25c\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5\nChange-Id: I582ee0634a8af5b71eb86d39b64f930b4df47730\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
